/Alt ()
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [7 8]
>>
endobj
670 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Subdirectories like `/usr/bin` store binaries, and `/usr/lib` holds libraries used by user-installed programs.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 16 0 R
>>
endobj
671 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (12. Process Information \(/proc\)  )
/Alt ()
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
672 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (A virtual file system that provides a view of kernel and process information. It dynamically updates and contains directories named after process IDs \(PIDs\). )
/Alt ()
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [10 11]
>>
endobj
673 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (For example, `/proc/cpuinfo` gives information about the CPU.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 16 0 R
>>
endobj
674 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (13. Mount Directory \(/mnt\)  )
/Alt ()
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
675 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (A temporary location where external storage devices \(e.g., additional hard drives, USB devices\) are mounted for access. Administrators often manually mount devices here for maintenance or temporary use.)
